# Queue contents are local runtime state, never committed.
data/
*.jsonl

# Node. The server itself still has zero runtime dependencies; the /v2
# Hono+OpenAPI proof-of-concept (see HONO-POC.md) added real ones, so the
# lockfile is now committed for reproducible installs.
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*

# ocli's local profile/spec cache, created by `npx ocli profiles add` when
# generating a CLI against /v2/openapi.json — machine-local test state.
.ocli/

# Editor / OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Local overrides
.env
.env.*
docker-compose.override.yml

# Agent-harness config. As of 2026-08-29 this repo is the HOME of the
# coordinator protocol (.claude/skills/relay-coordinator/) and the default-deny
# security guard (.claude/hooks/coordinator-guard.js), so those two must be
# VERSIONED — this used to be a blanket `.claude/` exclusion, which would have
# silently left the whole protocol untracked after the move.
#
# Everything else under .claude/ is still machine-local and never published:
# permission allowlists accrete literal command lines from real sessions, and
# coordinator-violations.log records whatever an agent was sending when it was
# blocked, including personal messages.
.claude/*
!.claude/hooks/
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/settings.json.bak-pre-default-deny

# ...but re-exclude local state inside the directories re-included above.
.claude/**/*.log
.claude/**/*.local.json
.claude/.guard-mainthread-seen

# Build output of the API description. `openapi.json` is the AUTHORED source of
# truth and stays committed; `openapi.yaml` is derived from it by openapi-yaml.js,
# which server.js renders per request rather than reading this file (see the
# comment at server.js:4743) - so nothing at runtime ever opens it. Committing it
# would be committing build output that can only drift from the JSON.
/openapi.yaml

# Scratch mutant copies of server.js, written next to it (not in the OS temp
# dir) so its relative requires (./icons.js, ./push.js, ./share.js) resolve.
# tools/seat-unwatched-selftest.js cleans these up itself; ignored here too in
# case a killed test run leaves one behind.
*.mutant.js
